/* The world's coastline, so the map is a place rather than a field of dots.

   Natural Earth land polygons, which are public domain (CC0). Two sources:
   the game spends its first hours over the Irish Sea, where 1:50m draws
   Britain as a handful of blocks, so anything that fits wholly inside
   Europe comes from 1:10m and everything else from 1:50m. Nothing is drawn
   twice because a ring is taken from one set or the other, never both.

   Boiled down to fit in a page a phone loads over a mobile connection:
   simplified to a kilometre or so at home and four abroad, the smallest
   islands dropped, coordinates quantised to hundredths of a degree and
   written as zig-zag deltas in base 64. A megabyte of GeoJSON becomes
   eighty-six kilobytes of this. A bracketed run is one number of several
   digits.

   It lives in its own file rather than inside stopover.html because it is
   data, it never changes, and the worker can cache it once. */
